      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the values of \\( y \\in [0, \\pi] \\) for which the inequality \\(\\sin(x+y) \\leq \\sin(x) + \\sin(y)\\) holds for all \\( x \\in [0, \\pi] \\), we will analyze the inequality step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Use the angle addition formula for sine\nThe angle addition formula for sine is:\n\\[\n\\sin(x+y) = \\sin(x)\\cos(y) + \\cos(x)\\sin(y)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Substitute the angle addition formula into the inequality\nSubstitute \\(\\sin(x+y)\\) into the given inequality:\n\\[\n\\sin(x)\\cos(y) + \\cos(x)\\sin(y) \\leq \\sin(x) + \\sin(y)\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Rearrange the inequality\nRewrite the inequality to group terms involving \\(\\sin(x)\\) and \\(\\cos(x)\\):\n\\[\n\\sin(x)\\cos(y) - \\sin(x) \\leq \\sin(y) - \\cos(x)\\sin(y)\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Factor out common terms\nFactor out \\(\\sin(x)\\) on the left side and \\(\\sin(y)\\) on the right side:\n\\[\n\\sin(x)(\\cos(y) - 1) \\leq \\sin(y)(1 - \\cos(x))\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Analyze the inequality for different regions\nWe need to analyze the inequality for different regions of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) within the interval \\([0, \\pi]\\).\n\n#### Case 1: \\(x = 0\\)\nIf \\(x = 0\\), the inequality becomes:\n\\[\n\\sin(0)\\cos(y) - \\sin(0) \\leq \\sin(y)(1 - \\cos(0))\n\\]\n\\[\n0 \\leq \\sin(y)(1 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n0 \\leq 0\n\\]\nThis is always true, so the inequality holds for all \\(y \\in [0, \\pi]\\).\n\n#### Case 2: \\(y = 0\\)\nIf \\(y = 0\\), the inequality becomes:\n\\[\n\\sin(x) \\cos(0) + \\cos(x) \\sin(0) \\leq \\sin(x) + \\sin(0)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin(x) \\leq \\sin(x)\n\\]\nThis is always true, so the inequality holds for all \\(x \\in [0, \\pi]\\) and \\(y = 0\\).\n\n#### Case 3: \\(x = \\pi\\)\nIf \\(x = \\pi\\), the inequality becomes:\n\\[\n\\sin(\\pi + y) \\leq \\sin(\\pi) + \\sin(y)\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin(\\pi + y) = -\\sin(y)\\), we have:\n\\[\n-\\sin(y) \\leq 0 + \\sin(y)\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\sin(y) \\leq \\sin(y)\n\\]\nThis inequality holds if and only if \\(\\sin(y) \\geq 0\\). Within the interval \\([0, \\pi]\\), \\(\\sin(y) \\geq 0\\) for \\(y \\in [0, \\pi]\\).\n\n### Conclusion\nCombining all the cases, we see that the inequality \\(\\sin(x+y) \\leq \\sin(x) + \\sin(y)\\) holds for all \\(x \\in [0, \\pi]\\) and \\(y \\in [0, \\pi]\\). Therefore, the solution is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{[0, \\pi]}\n\\]",
